<title>SWITZERLAND: Zurich mulls U.S. listing.</title>
<headline>Zurich mulls U.S. listing.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Zurich Group is making internal preparations for a possible listing in the U.S. and is likely to make a decision in mid-1998 on a move to the New York Stock Exchange, chief executive Rolf Hueppi said.</p>
<p>&quot;The preparation on this is underway...we are interested in a global spread of shareholders,&quot; he told a news conference.</p>
<p>He said the plan called for the company to report 1998 results according to the GAP (General Accounting Principles) required for listing in the U.S.</p>
<p>Hueppi said if the company decided in favour of a U.S. listing, it would probably target 1999 for the actual initial listing. -- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
